## 1. Direct answer

The section **still exists** — it is `src/components/layout/WorkspacesSection.vue`, mounted in `DesktopSidebar.vue`. You don't see it because of **three hidden gates**, one of which is exactly the mode filter you asked me to remove last turn:

| Gate | Where | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `v-if="!isCompanyMode"` | `DesktopSidebar.vue` | In **company mode** the whole section is not rendered at all |
| `workspacesExpanded: false` | `WorkspacesSection.vue` `data()` | Only the `WORKSPACES` header row shows; the apps list stays folded |
| `v-if="hasWorkspaceApps"` (root) | `WorkspacesSection.vue` | With **no workspace apps in the active project** nothing renders — not even the header |

And `workspaceApps` is **not** an apps-registry list; it is data-driven:

```
DesktopSidebar.workspaceApps  →  $storex.projects.projectApps            (store/project.js)
                              →  state.workspaces ([] by default)
                              →  set ONLY in activeProjectChanged: state.workspaces = API.allWorkspaces
```

So the section is only populated **after a project activation**. No workspaces on the backend (`/api/workspaces`) ⇒ empty list ⇒ no section.

There is a second, always-available entry: **Main menu (avatar / footer) → Workspaces** (`src/components/main-menu/WorkspacesMenu.vue`), with per-workspace app submenus, `New workspace` and `Manage workspaces`.

## 2. Recommendation

Restore the sidebar section unfiltered (consistent with the "always show all options" decision) and default it **expanded**, so the apps are visible without a click. Leave the `hasWorkspaceApps` guard: rendering an empty "Workspaces" header would be noise.

## 3. Changes summary

| File | Change | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `src/components/layout/DesktopSidebar.vue` | Removed the `v-if="!isCompanyMode"` gate on `<WorkspacesSection>`; removed the now-unused `isCompanyMode` computed; comment updated to describe real behaviour | Mode filter was hiding the launcher |
| `src/components/layout/WorkspacesSection.vue` | `workspacesExpanded: false` → `true` | Apps were one hidden click away (the "where are they?" symptom) |

