## 4. Anti-patterns avoided / to avoid

- ❌ **Filtering a launcher by mode** — it creates "where did my menu go" support tickets. Permission gates (`Infrastructure` → `$users.isAdmin`) are legitimate; product-mode gates are not.
- ❌ **Collapsed-by-default sections** — folding primary navigation hides the feature entirely on first run.
- ❌ **Rendering an empty section header** — keep `v-if="hasWorkspaceApps"`; an empty "WORKSPACES" label is worse than none.

## 5. Accessibility checklist

- [x] Workspace app buttons are real `<button>`s (Tab reachable, Enter/Space activate).
- [x] The section toggle keeps `title="Toggle Workspaces"` and a `fa-chevron-up/down` icon → non-color state cue.
- [x] Collapsed rail keeps `:title="app.name"`, so icon-only mode still exposes the label.
- [x] Selection state is `bg-white/10 + text-base-content` (contrast change, not color-only).
- [ ] Not addressed here: `aria-expanded` on the section toggle — worth adding if you want full parity with the `APPS` header.

## 6. Implementation steps

1. Deploy the two files above.
2. Reload — the section now appears **regardless of `workspace_mode`**, with its apps expanded.
3. If it is **still absent**, the active project has no workspace apps: check `GET /api/workspaces` and that `projects.workspaces` is filled (`state.workspaces = API.allWorkspaces` runs only inside `activeProjectChanged`).
4. Fallback entry always available: **footer avatar → Workspaces** → `Manage workspaces` (creates/edits them; registered as app `workspaces`).

Want me to also (a) add `aria-expanded` to both section toggles, and (b) surface `Workspaces`/`Manage workspaces` as an `APPS` entry so the manager is reachable even when the active project has zero workspace apps?

